    "title": "OpenStreetMap: a daily budget (a quarter of the public limits) and a 3-month cache, set in Thresholds & gates",
    "why": "Jason, 2026-11-14 (through the session manager): a town and kind OpenStreetMap answered isn't asked again for 3 months (was 30 days for the crawler and the site's nearby spots); our Overpass use stays at a quarter of the public guidance, 2,500 queries and 250 MB a day, the crawler up to 1,500 and the site up to 1,000, halved while any OpenStreetMap server bans us and for 14 days after the last ban lifts. Each is a setting in Thresholds & gates (osm_daily_crawler, osm_daily_site, osm_daily_mb, osm_cache_days, osm_ramp_days). ServiceHealth::osmBudget counts the day (UTC) in osm_usage (migration 2026-11-14_osm_usage); the crawler's plan sends its share (at most about half an hour's worth a run) and its report counts what it used; the site's OpenPlaces::overpass stops when its share is used. FAQ entry updated.",
